Structure location plans, if required pursuant to Section 8-6-26(e) shall contain the following elements:
(a) Structure location and drainage plans shall be prepared, signed and sealed by a land surveyor, professional engineer, or landscape architect registered in the state, drawn to scale and may be shown on a certified boundary survey of the lot or any other drawing showing the information required below.
(b) The structure location and drainage plan shall be a drawing with sufficient readability and accuracy to ensure that the proposed improvements will be constructed on the lot in conformance with the requirements of these subdivision regulations, or other regulations as applicable.
(c) Structure location and drainage plans shall show the following, as applicable:
(1) Prepared on a minimum 11x17 sheet size;
(2) Boundary lines of the lot, giving distances to the nearest one-tenth of a foot and bearings to the nearest minute;
(3) Location and names of all abutting streets or other rights-of-way;
(4) Minimum required front, side and rear building setback or buffer lines with dimensions and notation of the existing zoning on the property;
(5) The location of all buildings with finished floor elevations, driveways, parking areas, swimming pools, recreational courts, patios, accessory structures and other improvements existing or proposed on the property, and dimensions of buildings and distances between all structures and the nearest property lines;
(6) All easements, public water, sewer or storm drainage facilities traversing or located on the property, septic tank and septic tank drain field;
(7) Subdivision name, lot designation, land lot, district, address, and tax parcel ID number;
(8) North arrow and graphic and numeric scale;
(9) Limit of the 100-year floodplain, wetland areas, streams, historic structures and any applicable buffers or special building setback lines;
(10) All other applicable requirements of these subdivision regulations or conditions of zoning approval;
(11) Name, address and telephone number of the owner and the person who prepared the structure location plan; and
(12) Existing and proposed grades with two feet contour intervals, arrows showing path of drainage with proposed improvements, and erosion and sediment control measures as required.
(d) The following note shall appear on all structure location and drainage plans:
"This Structure Location and Drainage Plan has been reviewed for general compliance with the City of Conyers Subdivision Regulations and is approved for issuance of a building permit for the residential structure and other improvements shown hereon. This approval is granted with the provision that no certificate of occupancy shall be issued until conformance to this structure location and drainage plan has been field verified by an as-built survey and certification prepared, signed, and sealed by a land surveyor, professional engineer, or landscape architect registered in the State of Georgia."
(e) The structure location and drainage as-built survey shall contain all items as specified in subsection C of this section.
(f) The following note shall appear on all structure location and drainage as-built surveys:
"I, ___________, a qualified registered Professional ________ (Engineer, Surveyor, or Landscape Architect) in the state of Georgia, hereby certify with my signature and seal, that I have made sufficient visits to the construction site and to the best of my knowledge, the structures located at ___________ in land lot ___, of the ___ district of Rockdale County, Georgia, have been constructed in substantial compliance with the approved Structure Location and Drainage Plan for the above listed project.
This ___ day of _____, 20___.
___________
[Signature] [Seal]
GA Registration No. _______"
(Code 1990, § 8-6-68; Ord. No. 757, 6-20-2007; Ord. No. 1273, § 1, 11-17-2021)

